<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14408" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dissĭmŭlātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				dissembling</i>, <i>concealing</i>, <i>disguising</i>, <i>dissimulation</i>
			(good prose). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> In gen.,
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Off. 3, 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. de Or. 2, 67</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 6,
				3, 85</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 11, 26</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">veste servili in dissimulationem sui
					compositus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 13, 25</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id.
				H. 4, 18</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. A. 6, 18 <i>fin.</i></span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In partic., <i>the Socratic</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰρωνεία</span>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic. Ac. 2, 5, 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 9,
				1, 29</span></i>; but too restricted for that idea, acc. to <i><span class="en">Quint. 9,
				2, 44</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A disregarding</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep.
				9, 13, 21</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In late Lat., <i>negligence</i>, <i>carelessness</i>, <i><span class="en">Veg. Vet.
				6</span></i> prooem. § 1; so ib. § 3;
					<i><span class="en">id. Mil. 1, 18</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
